WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Our universities are failing.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
When the Fifteenth Amendment
to the Constitution was passed,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.300
which university's students stood
in the streets and protested?

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.500
Which university's teachers took to the streets?

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.500
Is the duty of university students
only to become bureaucrats?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.700
Is the duty of teachers only to give
lectures in class as a mere formality?

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.700
No! Bangladesh's academia has failed.

NOTE paragraph

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.880
Look at Harvard. Harvard did not stop, even when
Donald Trump threatened to cut its funding.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.260
Oxford has been serving the people
for a thousand years.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.980
Look at Socrates. He walked the streets,
explaining to people what their rights were.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.000
What are you doing, and what am I doing?
